  "rules": [
    "When the model forecasts a steady upward trend (e.g., +0.30/30d) while recent history shows high volatility and negative sentiment spikes, apply a mean reversion correction of -15% to -25% against the forecasted path.",
    "If the true outcome drops significantly below the model's first 7-day forecast (e.g., >5 EUR deviation), reduce all subsequent daily forecasts by an additional 0.80-1.20 EUR/day to account for momentum lag.",
    "The model consistently overestimates short-term recovery after a crash; apply a downward bias of -3% to the first 10 days of any forecast when sentiment history contains recent negative spikes (-1.00).",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.00) but volatility is high, the model's linear extrapolation fails; switch to a stochastic correction that reduces daily growth rates by 40% until volatility stabilizes.",
    "In periods of low sentiment and high historical variance, the model's 'smooth' trajectory should be truncated after day 5, as true outcomes typically remain flat or decline rather than rising."
  ]
}
